# Converted to the revised ten-section template (plus section 11); content and tables carried from the previous version.
BOOK = '2 Timothy'
TESTAMENT = 'New Testament'
GENRE = 'letters'
SUBTITLE = 'Hold Fast, Rightly Divide, and Finish the Course'
SECTIONS = [(1, 'Book Setting & Program Identity', [('p', 'This section introduces you to the book by explaining who wrote it, who received it, and what was happening when it was written. It also shows you which of God’s programs the book belongs to — Israel’s prophetic program or the Body of Christ’s mystery program. Knowing the setting and the program identity helps you read the book in its proper context and understand how its teachings fit into the larger story of Scripture.'), ('p', '2 Timothy is a letter from “Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ by the will of God, according to the promise of life which is in Christ Jesus” to “Timothy, my dearly beloved son” (2 Tim. 1:1–2). Paul writes from prison near the end of his course. He urges Timothy to stir up the gift of God, to endure hardness, to hold the form of sound words, and to preach the word.'), ('box', 'Program Identity:', '2 Timothy is Paul’s last letter in the pastoral group, written to a younger minister. It is read for what it says about endurance, doctrine, and Scripture. This reading rests on the letter’s own audience markers and setting.')]),
(2, 'Narrative Flow of 2 Timothy', [('p', 'This section gives you a simple walkthrough of how the book unfolds. Instead of diving into details right away, it shows the major movements in the letter — how Paul begins, how his instructions develop, and how the letter builds toward its close. Seeing the flow of the book helps you understand the big picture before you study the individual passages.'), ('h3', 'Movement 1 — Stir Up the Gift (Ch. 1)'), ('p', 'Paul gives thanks for Timothy’s faith, tells him not to be ashamed of the testimony, and recalls grace given in Christ Jesus before the world began (2 Tim. 1:3–14).'), ('h3', 'Movement 2 — Endure and Rightly Divide (Ch. 2)'), ('p', 'Paul calls Timothy to be strong, to commit what he heard to faithful men, to endure as a soldier, and to study to be approved, rightly dividing the word of truth (2 Tim. 2:1–26).'), ('h3', 'Movement 3 — Perilous Times and the Scriptures (Ch. 3)'), ('p', 'Paul describes perilous times in the last days and urges Timothy to continue in what he has learned from Scripture (2 Tim. 3:1–17).'), ('h3', 'Movement 4 — Preach the Word and Finish the Course (Ch. 4)'), ('p', 'Paul charges Timothy to preach the word, speaks of his own departure, and says he has kept the faith (2 Tim. 4:1–22).')]),
(3, 'Program Themes in 2 Timothy', [('p', 'This section highlights the major ideas Paul emphasizes in this book — the big doctrinal themes that shape how the Body of Christ should think and live. These themes are not verse-by-verse explanations; they are the book’s main emphases, the repeated ideas Paul wants believers to carry forward. Seeing these themes together helps you understand the book’s message before you look at the individual truths in the tables.'), ('ol', ['<b>Not the Spirit of Fear</b> — “God hath not given us the spirit of fear; but of power, and of love, and of a sound mind” (2 Tim. 1:7).', '<b>Faithful Men</b> — The things heard are to be committed to faithful men able to teach others (2 Tim. 2:2).', '<b>Rightly Dividing</b> — “Study to shew thyself approved unto God, a workman that needeth not to be ashamed, rightly dividing the word of truth” (2 Tim. 2:15).', '<b>All Scripture</b> — “All scripture is given by inspiration of God, and is profitable for doctrine” (2 Tim. 3:16).', '<b>Preach the Word</b> — Paul charges Timothy to preach the word in season and out of season (2 Tim. 4:2).'])]),
(4, 'Christ in 2 Timothy', [('p', 'This section gathers what the letter teaches about Christ — who He is, what He has done, and how Paul presents Him to the church. These statements help you see the book’s Christ-centered focus before you study the doctrinal truths in detail. By collecting these verses together, you get a clear picture of how 2 Timothy lifts up Christ.'), ('ol', ['<b>Christ Jesus Who Abolished Death</b> — Our Saviour Jesus Christ has abolished death and brought life and immortality to light through the gospel (2 Tim. 1:10).', '<b>Of the Seed of David</b> — “Remember that Jesus Christ of the seed of David was raised from the dead according to my gospel” (2 Tim. 2:8).', '<b>The Sure Foundation</b> — “The foundation of God standeth sure” (2 Tim. 2:19).', '<b>The Righteous Judge</b> — The Lord, the righteous judge, shall give a crown (2 Tim. 4:8).', '<b>The Lord Stood With Me</b> — “The Lord stood with me, and strengthened me” (2 Tim. 4:17).'])]),
(5, 'The Church, the Law, and Israel in 2 Timothy', [('p', 'This section helps you see how 2 Timothy speaks about the church, the law, and Israel without mixing their programs. By gathering these points together, this section shows you how to read 2 Timothy in its own setting — as a Body-of-Christ letter — while recognizing what it says (and does not say) about Israel’s program.'), ('p', 'The letter speaks of the seed of David and of Paul’s gospel without placing believers inside Israel’s covenants:'), ('ul', ['Paul says Jesus Christ was “of the seed of David” and raised from the dead “according to my gospel” (2 Tim. 2:8). The study reports the text as written.', 'Paul says he endures “for the elect’s sakes” (2 Tim. 2:10) and, “If we suffer, we shall also reign with him” (2 Tim. 2:12). The study reports these as written and builds no wider doctrine on them.', 'The “holy calling” in 2 Timothy 1:9 is reported as written, with grace given “in Christ Jesus before the world began.”', 'The letter does not place believers under any Israelite covenant.']), ('p', 'This reading rests on the letter’s own audience markers and setting.')]),
(6, 'Body-of-Christ Distinctions', [('p', 'This section highlights the teachings in 2 Timothy that belong uniquely to the Body of Christ — truths Paul gives to the church in this present age. By gathering these together, this section helps you see how 2 Timothy contributes to the doctrine and order of the Body of Christ without borrowing from Israel’s prophetic program.'), ('p', '2 Timothy teaches endurance and faithfulness in doctrine:'), ('ul', ['power, love, and a sound mind', 'teaching committed to faithful men', 'rightly dividing the word of truth', 'Scripture profitable for doctrine, reproof, correction, and instruction', 'a finished course and a kept faith']), ('p', 'It does not state which future events lie behind the “last days” it names beyond what the letter says.')]),
(7, 'Truths Table: What 2 Timothy Says', [('p', 'This table gathers the key statements, instructions, and teachings in 2 Timothy and shows which ones belong to the Body of Christ. Each row lists a truth from the letter, explains what it says, and identifies its program identity based on Paul’s audience and setting. This helps you see, at a glance, what 2 Timothy teaches directly to the church today and keeps those truths separate from universal principles or reports that apply more broadly.'), ('p', 'Program Identity shows where a truth belongs. “Body of Christ (Pauline) Truth” marks a statement, command, warning or instruction given to the Body of Christ through Paul.'), ('table', ['Category', 'Truth Revealed in 2 Timothy', 'Program Identity', 'Scripture'], [['A Holy Calling', 'God saved us and called us according to His own purpose and grace.', 'Body of Christ (Pauline) Truth', '2 Tim. 1:9'], ['Death Abolished', 'Christ hath abolished death and brought life to light.', 'Body of Christ (Pauline) Truth', '2 Tim. 1:10'], ['Rightly Dividing', 'Study to show thyself approved, rightly dividing the word of truth.', 'Body of Christ (Pauline) Truth', '2 Tim. 2:15'], ['Scripture Inspired', 'All scripture is given by inspiration of God.', 'Body of Christ (Pauline) Truth', '2 Tim. 3:16'], ['A Finished Course', 'I have fought a good fight, I have finished my course.', 'Body of Christ (Pauline) Truth', '2 Tim. 4:7'], ['The Seed of David', 'Jesus Christ of the seed of David raised from the dead.', 'Body of Christ (Pauline) Truth', '2 Tim. 2:8'], ['Suffer and Reign', 'If we suffer, we shall also reign with him.', 'Body of Christ (Pauline) Truth', '2 Tim. 2:12'], ['Last Days', 'In the last days perilous times shall come.', 'Body of Christ (Pauline) Truth', '2 Tim. 3:1']], [20, 36, 26, 18])]),
(8, 'Universal Truths Table (All People, All Time)', [('p', 'This table gathers the truths in 2 Timothy that apply to everyone, not just the Body of Christ. These are principles rooted in God’s character — things that hold true across all programs and all ages. By separating these universal truths from Paul’s program-specific instructions, this section helps you see what 2 Timothy teaches all believers everywhere and what it teaches the church in its own setting.'), ('table', ['Universal Truth', 'Description', 'Scripture'], [['Power, Love, Sound Mind', 'God hath not given us the spirit of fear.', '2 Tim. 1:7'], ['Endure Hardness', 'Endure hardness, as a good soldier of Jesus Christ.', '2 Tim. 2:3'], ['Flee Youthful Lusts', 'Follow righteousness, faith, charity, peace.', '2 Tim. 2:22'], ['Gentle Correction', 'The servant of the Lord must be gentle unto all men.', '2 Tim. 2:24'], ['Inspired Scripture', 'Scripture is profitable for doctrine, reproof, correction, instruction.', '2 Tim. 3:16'], ['Preach the Word', 'Be instant in season, out of season.', '2 Tim. 4:2'], ['Keep the Faith', 'I have kept the faith.', '2 Tim. 4:7'], ['Continue in What You Learned', 'Continue thou in the things which thou hast learned.', '2 Tim. 3:14']], [30, 46, 24])]),
(9, 'Program-Safe Application Grid', [('p', 'This section shows how to apply the teachings of 2 Timothy without mixing programs. The applications come directly from Paul’s instructions to the Body of Christ and from the universal truths that apply to everyone. By keeping the applications tied to what the letter actually says — and not borrowing commands from Israel’s covenants or prophetic program — this grid helps you respond to 2 Timothy in a way that is faithful to its setting, clear, and safe.'), ('ol', ['<b>Stir up the gift</b> — Not fear, but power, love, and a sound mind (2 Tim. 1:6–7).', '<b>Hold the form of sound words</b> — Keep what was heard (2 Tim. 1:13).', '<b>Teach faithful men</b> — Pass the teaching on (2 Tim. 2:2).', '<b>Rightly divide the word</b> — Study to be approved (2 Tim. 2:15).', '<b>Be gentle in correction</b> — Instruct opponents in meekness (2 Tim. 2:24–25).', '<b>Continue in Scripture</b> — Hold to what was learned (2 Tim. 3:14–17).', '<b>Preach the word</b> — Reprove, rebuke, exhort (2 Tim. 4:2).', '<b>Finish the course</b> — Keep the faith (2 Tim. 4:7).'])]),
(10, 'Teaching Outline for 2 Timothy', [('p', 'This outline gives you a teacher-ready structure for presenting the book. It follows the narrative movements and highlights the major themes, making it easy to teach 2 Timothy in classes, small groups, or personal study.'), ('olr', ['Stir Up the Gift (Ch. 1) — Power, love, and a sound mind. <i>(2 Tim. 1:6–14)</i>', 'A Soldier, an Athlete, a Husbandman (2:1–13) — Endurance. <i>(2 Tim. 2:1–13)</i>', 'A Workman Approved (2:14–26) — Rightly dividing and gentle correction. <i>(2 Tim. 2:15, 24–25)</i>', 'Perilous Times (3:1–9) — The last days. <i>(2 Tim. 3:1–9)</i>', 'The Scriptures (3:10–17) — Continue in what was learned. <i>(2 Tim. 3:14–17)</i>', 'Preach the Word (4:1–8) — The charge and the crown. <i>(2 Tim. 4:1–8)</i>', 'Personal Words (4:9–22) — Companions and the Lord who stood with Paul. <i>(2 Tim. 4:9–22)</i>'])]),
(11, 'Companion Usage and Study Suggestions', [('h3', 'How to Use This Companion in Personal Study'), ('p', 'This Companion is designed to walk alongside you as you read 2 Timothy, helping you see both what the letter says and the timeless truths rooted in God’s character. Use it slowly, chapter by chapter, letting the narrative movements, themes, and truths deepen your understanding. The Program-Safe Applications draw only on what 2 Timothy itself says, so your response stays tied to the text.'), ('h3', 'How to Use This Companion in Small Groups or Classes'), ('p', 'This Companion provides a clear, structured framework that makes teaching 2 Timothy simple and accessible. Each section gives you ready-to-use material: narrative movements for overview, program themes for doctrinal clarity, universal truths for discussion, and a pastoral teaching outline for weekly lessons. Use the tables to help your group see what the letter states and what it leaves unsaid, and use the Program-Safe Application Grid to foster meaningful, Christ-centered conversation.'), ('h3', 'How This Companion Fits Within the Acts Overlap Theology Series'), ('p', 'This Companion is part of a larger series designed to help believers read every book of Scripture without blurring God’s prophetic program for Israel and His mystery program for the Body of Christ. Within the Acts Overlap framework, 2 Timothy was written during the overlap from Paul to a younger minister. This Companion shows you how to read its charges in their own setting while drawing out the principles that apply to all believers.')])]
